hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2755","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn al-'Ala' ibn Kurayb, narrated to us Mu'awiyah ibn Hisham, narrated to us Sufyan al-Thawri, on the authority of Ja'far ibn Muhammad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Jabir ibn 'Abd Allah, who mentioned the lengthy hadith about the Hajj of the Prophet (ﷺ), and he said:\n\n*\"Then he (the Prophet ﷺ) performed Tawaf (circuit) quickly for three rounds and walked normally for four rounds. Then he came to the Maqam (Station of Ibrahim), and recited: 'And take, [O believers], from the standing place of Ibrahim a place of prayer' (Quran 2:125). He placed the Maqam between himself and the door. When he finished, he came to the House (Ka'bah) and touched the corner (al-Rukn).\"*\n\nThe rest of the hadith was mentioned.\n\n**CHAPTER:**"
